{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7677","id":5211203474,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABNpynkg","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7677","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7677.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7677.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7677","number":7677,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"docs(id): Joplin importer design against the #2048 object model (#5848)","user":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Design record for #5848: importing Joplin into the #2048 object model.\n\n`doc/2026-11-08_design_id5848.md` — design only, no importer code. It consumes the #2048 model as landed (`doc/2026-11-01_design_id2048.md`, PR #3885) and does not re-decide it; the one place it touches a parent decision (which head exports for a multi-head note) is recorded explicitly in §7 of the doc.\n\nSettled:\n\n- **Mapping** — Joplin notes → logical notes (`note.create`, new ID identity, Joplin ID kept only in a persisted import manifest); notebooks → collection notes with typed membership references; tags → observed-remove tag claims, verbatim; to-dos → notes with to-do claims; resources → content blobs with a resource record (filename/MIME as claims).\n- **Links** — `:/<note-id>` body references rewritten to structured typed references via the manifest (note vs resource ID spaces kept distinct); dangling references degrade to stored surface + unresolved state, per #2048, and are counted in the import report.\n- **Round-trip contract** — export back to JEX stated as canonical set equalities (notes, per-note tag sets, link targets, notebook tree, attachment byte hashes), with an explicit lossy list (revision history, plugin markup interpretation, encrypted items, unexported concurrent heads).\n- **Invariants** — stable ID identity, append-only import with explicit head-joining on re-import, idempotency via the manifest, no silent drops (full import accounting), no E2EE key handling.\n- **Test corpus plan** — synthetic generated fixtures plus round-trip and idempotency properties; the oracle is canonical set equality modulo the stated lossy list.\n- **Rejected alternatives** — per-`document.put` import, Markdown-only import without a manifest, and Joplin sync-target emulation for v1, each with reasons.\n- **Splits filed and linked:** #7675 (Joplin revision-history import), #7676 (continuous sync target vs one-shot import).\n\nCloses #5848\n\nQueue: task 12987 (repo-health-code-pilot), lane code-e. Closure route is the one the issue and packet specify: a merged PR carrying a closing keyword, with the decision record in `doc/` linked from the issue.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796731989&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7677&ref=